comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-05T10:28:03.891Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: request-specific live search plus strict full all-status corpus 2889/2889 with zero omissions and current open/in_progress inventories found no owner for this explicit-selector overhead policy. Four completed receipt predecessors and the open whole-response budget parent were read in full. This canonical intake preserves their shipped scopes and requires implementation before closure."
  "2026-10-06T04:53:43.326Z","harness:codex","Live continuation scope: complete strict corpus 2894/2894 with zero unreadable records, omissions or truncation; selected full metadata and verified complete history read. Deliver composed read ceilings, deliberate-field omission cost, executable projection recovery and prepared source-map/worker privacy repairs in one PR. Only these five owners are active. No duplicate intake created. Auto-release run37414884541 failed specifically on source-map-js before publication; patched lock is part of this delivery."
  "2026-10-06T04:59:32.759Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: original implementation fails the same newly extended primary fixtures before source correction. Combined ceiling resumes refuse read_output_cursor_stale and the positional coordinate is19 where14 is required; explicit status receipts include deliberately excluded children/claim_state; full/global selector recovery repeats its invalid invocation. After correction, original uncapped collection state drives cursor fingerprints and offsets, explicit selectors define receipt scope, and global selector removal preserves command-local mode placement. Real persisted temporary trackers and existing transport matrices own the proof, without new production test seams or duplicate suites. Final full coverage and hosted review remain pending."
  "2026-10-06T05:01:46.786Z","harness:codex","Explicit-selection policy preserves the original complete receipt shape and scopes it to the caller-selected answer, rather than listing deliberately excluded groups. Default/depth restoration remains material. Retained schedule/artifact regression tables now assert the actual persisted requested alias values independently, including requested empty collections; they still prove unselected placeholders carry no payload. Removed the now unreachable explicit-selector attribution branch from default/depth materiality. Budget/string/row truncation keeps separate shared evidence."
  "2026-10-06T05:17:26.946Z","harness:codex","The retained real materiality fixture now checks selected status and item.status, canonical ID, requested empty notes/tests/docs and attributed dependency projections. Reconstruct the prior receipt around the same selected payload and require the emitted answer to use under70 percent of those bytes. Existing scheduling/artifact regression cases continue to verify actual requested reminder/event/deadline and artifact values; default and depth material omission/provenance receipts stay covered. Pure generic caller-supplied projection contracts remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-06T05:28:13.203Z","harness:codex","Canonical full-source run retained failure receipt:9780 pass/2 fail/2 platform skips across776 files. The changed explicit-field policy exposes one stale CLI/SDK alias parity expectation (children was previously reported deliberately omitted), and the independent consistency control still anchors the removed hasOmittedDependencyProvenance helper. Its negative source mutation cannot match and leaves3 control-script branches/1 statement uncovered. Retain all15 safe and15 assertion-sensitive unsafe controls; update the first two anchors to independently test default withheld attribution and full restoration, without deleting controls or weakening source coverage. The default scheduling/artifact rows retain their material-alias negative controls."
  "2026-10-06T05:30:00.803Z","harness:codex","Isolated preview of the revised control anchors passes the unchanged negative controller contract: all15 controls execute selected real tests and exit1 from behavior AssertionError, including default attribution withholding, full restoration and default schedule/artifact aliases. No control is removed, no timeout changes, and source-match cardinality still must be exactly one. Await the active static run before applying the two retained fixture corrections to the checkout."
  "2026-10-06T06:16:41.378Z","harness:codex","Delivery evidence for PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1412: fresh canonical coverage passed 9,782 tests with two platform skips; all 764 executable coverage rows and all 66,833 statements, 51,158 branches, 13,806 functions and 63,694 lines are fully covered, with zero skipped coverage counts. Four TypeScript projects, credential and doc-link checks, real packed Node/Bun/npx/bunx acceptance and unchanged security admission pass. Exact head 3af31b07b71d5892c03b200683cf2273628a2beb passed all 26 required hosted contexts, including the complete static command. Earlier failed local timing and stale-fixture receipts remain in history. All five initial bot artifacts were read, voted and specifically acknowledged; explicit source reviews remain pending and will be requested after closeout. Native default-branch alert retirement and exact public publication remain separate post-merge checks."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-06T05:31:35.103Z","harness:codex","Explicit field selectors define the requested answer. Omission materiality describes accidental loss or default/depth withholding, while deliberate selection should preserve only selected data, stable identity, requested empties and a compact complete receipt. Keep budget disclosure independent, and update genuine source-mutant controls whenever a policy removes their old anchor."
